  "note": "Operations 1 and 2/3 were submitted in two invocations of test/harness/upgrade-preview.ts: the first was interrupted by a Blockfrost evaluateTx refusal caused by its independently-advancing views (a confirmed transaction while the UTxO set still showed spent outputs), and the second resumed, skipping the two rotations already on chain. Both rotation hashes were verified present on chain before being folded into this record. The chain does not distinguish the two invocations; the order below is the order of submission.",
  "treeProvenance": "\u26a0 CORRECTED. These three trees are DECODED FROM THE CHAIN \u2014 each from the inline datum of the output that wrote it \u2014 not taken from the script's own intent. The resumed invocation had recorded `treeAtBootstrap` from its own starting state, which was already past both rotations, so the field described the wrong moment. Reading them back off the transactions that wrote them removes the question."
